# Database Rules

- Use Prisma and the existing PostgreSQL database.
- Preserve existing public models as source-of-truth submission data.
- New admin metadata models must not duplicate applicant PII.
- Use NOT NULL, UNIQUE, foreign keys, indexes, enums, and sensible defaults wherever appropriate.
- DriverApplicationAdmin.driverApplicationId must be UNIQUE and required.
- WarehouseApplicationAdmin.warehouseApplicationId must be UNIQUE and required.
- ContactAdmin.contactId must be UNIQUE and required.
- A successfully persisted application must have exactly one admin metadata record.
- Application + corresponding admin metadata must be created atomically in a PostgreSQL transaction.
- Do not apply destructive production migrations automatically.
- Verify migration state and backup/recovery assumptions before production changes.
- AuditLog must survive permanent deletion of application/contact records.
